From 5f4316003aee8e74fb48e29a86c6071d22ee5f86 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <168627+NeoTech@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 13:43:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(cli): --skill <folder|claude|copilot> install writes an
 AI agent skill

`camcraft-cli --skill <target> install [--dir <path>] [--user] [--force]`
writes a skill that teaches the CLI to an AI agent. The text has one
source: the body crates/app/src/cli_skill.md, then the CLI's own usage
texts (TOP_USAGE and each HELP_LANES entry), so the reference cannot
drift from the binary.

- folder: <dir>/SKILL.md
- claude: .claude/skills/camcraft-cli/SKILL.md (project; --user: home)
- copilot: .github/instructions/camcraft-cli.instructions.md

An existing file is refused with exit 1 unless --force is given.
Decisions in docs/decisions/3751-cli-skill-install.md.

Fixes #3751

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
